Description: Memory-safety hardening from -fanalyzer over remaining TUs
 - utils.c clean_environ(): 'var' was uninitialized and realloc()
   unchecked - first realloc() could free a wild pointer, a failure
   was followed by a NULL strncpy(). Now initialized and safely
   realloc'd, aborting sanitization on OOM.
 - acl.c: ipv6tmp leaked on the ACL-entry malloc failure; trim()
   called isspace() on signed chars (UB for high-bit bytes) and
   lacked NULL guards; the per-token malloc in parse_allowed_hosts()
   was unchecked (NULL dereference via trim()).
 - nrpe.c: isspace() on signed chars in the config parser (same UB).
 - check_nrpe.c: send/response packet calloc()s unchecked, and the
   v3/v4 response path could dereference a NULL v3_receive_packet
   when the server reply was malformed. The received buffer is now
   also force-terminated before printing ("%s" on wire data).
